# No AI Attribution

Do not mention AI, LLMs, Cursor, Copilot, ChatGPT, “AI-generated,” “AI-assisted,” or similar in any project artifact the user ships or publishes from this repo.

## Never put AI language in

- README, docs, comments, docstrings, CLI help, changelogs
- Commit messages, PR titles/bodies, tags, release notes
- Image/PNG/JPEG/EXIF metadata, `.license`, embeds, watermarks
- Config defaults, sample outputs, filenames, layer labels
- User-facing strings, errors, logs, or marketing copy in-repo

## Allowed

- The user may disclose AI use themselves on external websites; do not add that disclosure here.
- Internal `.cursor/` rules may discuss AI only as tooling instructions for the agent (this file).

## If asked to add attribution

Omit it. Prefer neutral wording (e.g. “procedural generator,” “starsky-gen,” contributor/copyright holder) with no AI reference.
